// B1 course (A2 → B1 roadmap), module 9 „Töö ja ametid” (a2b1-041…045), stage B1-. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline: the working life of the course's friends — Sofia's small
// logistics firm Tuul Logistika (boss Liis, logistician Markus, project leader Anna), Kadri's shifts at the children's
// ward of a Tallinn hospital, and Jaan, a café cook with evening shifts, who looks for a day job. Goal, said on the first
// sheet: at the end the learner applies for a job — a short application letter and a job interview (044 Kasuta).
//   041 Sofia's homework about her people's jobs (-na, vastutab … eest, tegeleb …-ga); Kadri on the radio; a career day
//       at Oskar's school (the learner presents a job and answers the children).
//   042 where is Anna? — the office phone (ma-forms with cases: lähen sööma / on kohtumas / tuleb söömast / jäi
//       vastamata); Jaan's way to a cook and Kadri's voice message; a Friday at the office in Sofia's place.
//   043 the firm looks for an administrator — the ad, ma- or da-infinitive after work verbs; three candidates;
//       Jelena's first day (role play and a memo).
//   044 Anna's interview a year ago — claim + example + link; Jaan is invited to the school canteen; the module project:
//       choose an ad, write the letter, go through the interview.
// B1 grammar added here (METHODOLOGY_STANDARD §7): the ma-infinitive with case endings -ma / -mas / -mast / -mata, taught
// in 042 and used again in 043 (notice, Avasta) and 044 (Anna's „käin kursusel õppimas”, Jaan's answers). Module 8's
// school vocabulary comes back (kool, tund, õpetaja, kodutöö, kursus, õppima, eksam, harjutama, aru saama, osalema,
// probleem, lahendus, julgema, huvitav, raske). Lesson 5 (045) is the module exam in Harno B1 form (unchanged). The v3
// file is in archive/v3/b1/module09.js, the v1 file in archive/v1/b1/module09.js.
